The bag should be easy to figure out. Apply it, if it makes
a monster it will self ID as a bag of tricks. You probably
should drop it on the minetown altar to discover its buc
status. Now pick up "throw away" stuff like rocks, armor,
weapons etc. until you are burdened. Now put all that junk
in the bag, if your status changes from burdened, it's a
BoH, if not it's an oilskin bag.

> So what should I wish for?

As others have mentioned, keeping the lamp is a viable
option, that's what I'm doing in my current game. I hate to
take the 20% chance the wish won't be granted and I like the
permanent light source. There's even a 5% chance it might
yield a hostile djinni which would probably be the most
challenging monster you've met to date.

An interesting twist for a really early wish is to go for an
artifact that you can't get otherwise. I assume at this
stage there are less than two artifacts in the game. If
you're Lawful, the Orb of Detection is cool, conferring
telepathy, MR, 1/2 spell damage (eventually the (OoF will
duplicate this) and toggle invisibility off and on.
Magicbane gives MR when wielded, will get you out of lot's
of tight spots if you aren't opposed to the E-word and catch
curses if you get far enough for that to be a problem.

If you are neutral, Grayswindir is a truly powerful weapon
you can't get otherwise. The Eyes of the Overworld gives MR,
astral vision and invoked enlightenment. The Platinum
Yendorian Express Card confers MR, telepathy and 1/2 spell
damage. Invoking is the same as an u?oCharging. The Eye of
the Aethiopica confers magic resistance, faster energy
regeneration and 1/2 spell damage. Wearing it grants
telepathy and invoking it gives a sort of level teleport
(between dungeon branches visited). While the (OoF grants
invoked level teleport, that doesn't help much unless you
acquire TC.
 
MB and Grayswindir will blast you 1/4 of the time for 4d4.
The other artifacts will blast you 4d10 every time. The
damage goes down by half once you have MR. Wishing,
wielding, invoking, picking up or wearing will cause
blasting so a wish for one of the quest artifacts with 40 HP
could be fatal.
